{"step_index":2116,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T04:54:14Z","thinking":"The Electron stack's core server component, an Express and WebSocket server, handles both static file serving and REST API endpoints. Static files are served from the `web/` directory through specific routes, and REST API calls manage application configuration, AI provider details, and Deepgram key interactions. Understanding this structure is essential for debugging and modifying the application's behavior.\n\n\nREST API endpoints facilitate provider verification, screenshot capture, window transparency, and always-on-top behavior. WebSocket communication handles interview initiation, audio streaming for transcription, vision analysis, preset switching, session resets, and automated turn detection leading to AI answer generation. The Electron main process configures the application window with transparency, always-on-top, and content protection, along with ghost mode functionality.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\src\\prompts\\interview.py","EndLine":140,"StartLine":50,"toolAction":"Viewing prompt logic","toolSummary":"View prompt guidelines"}}]}
{"step_index":2117,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T04:54:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-27T01:54:30-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-27T01:54:30-03:00\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/Documents/GitHub/Spectra/src/prompts/interview.py`\nTotal Lines: 467\nTotal Bytes: 20801\nShowing lines 50 to 140\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n50:     \r\n51:     prompt_parts = []\r\n52:     \r\n53:     # System role instructions\r\n54:     prompt_parts.append(\"\"\"You are an expert interview coach providing real-time assistance during a live job interview.\r\n55: Your goal is to help the candidate give the best possible answer to the interviewer's question.\r\n56: \r\n57: COMPREHENSIVE TECHNICAL INTERVIEW GUIDELINES:\r\n58: \r\n59: FOR CODING/ALGORITHM QUESTIONS:\r\n60: - Start with brief problem understanding and clarification\r\n61: - Provide intuitive explanation of the approach first\r\n62: - Give at least 2 different solutions when applicable (brute force → optimized)\r\n63: - Write clean, working code in the EXACT programming language specified\r\n64: - Include time and space complexity analysis for each approach\r\n65: - Explain the thought process and why you chose each approach\r\n66: - Add comments in code for clarity\r\n67: - Mention edge cases and how to handle them\r\n68: \r\n69: FOR DATA STRUCTURES & ALGORITHMS (DSA):\r\n70: - Explain which data structure/algorithm fits best and why\r\n71: - Discuss trade-offs between different approaches\r\n72: - Provide complexity analysis (Big O notation)\r\n73: - Include implementation details and optimizations\r\n74: - Mention real-world applications where this would be useful\r\n75: \r\n76: FOR SYSTEM DESIGN QUESTIONS:\r\n77: - Start with requirements gathering and clarification\r\n78: - Design high-level architecture first, then dive into components\r\n79: - Discuss scalability, reliability, and performance considerations\r\n80: - Choose appropriate databases, caching strategies, load balancing\r\n81: - Address bottlenecks and how to handle them\r\n82: - Include technology stack recommendations with justifications\r\n83: - Discuss monitoring, logging, and deployment strategies\r\n84: \r\n85: FOR TECHNICAL Q&A/CONCEPTS:\r\n86: - Provide clear, precise definitions\r\n87: - Explain use cases and practical applications\r\n88: - Compare with alternatives (pros/cons)\r\n89: - Give real-world examples from your experience\r\n90: - Mention best practices and common pitfalls\r\n91: - Include relevant technologies and frameworks\r\n92: \r\n93: FOR API DESIGN QUESTIONS:\r\n94: - Follow RESTful principles and industry standards\r\n95: - Design proper URL structure and HTTP methods\r\n96: - Include request/response examples with JSON schemas\r\n97: - Discuss authentication, authorization, and security\r\n98: - Address versioning, rate limiting, and error handling\r\n99: - Consider scalability and performance optimizations\r\n100: \r\n101: FOR FRONTEND/BACKEND TECHNICAL QUESTIONS:\r\n102: - Mention specific frameworks, libraries, and tools\r\n103: - Discuss performance optimizations and best practices\r\n104: - Include code examples when relevant\r\n105: - Address cross-browser compatibility, responsive design (frontend)\r\n106: - Discuss security, databases, and architecture patterns (backend)\r\n107: \r\n108: GENERAL APPROACH:\r\n109: - Always be authentic and use real experiences from the candidate's background\r\n110: - Structure answers clearly with logical flow\r\n111: - Be concise but comprehensive - avoid unnecessary fluff\r\n112: - Show depth of knowledge while remaining practical\r\n113: - Demonstrate problem-solving thinking process\"\"\")\r\n114:     \r\n115:     # PERSISTENT CANDIDATE CONTEXT - Always present, never removed\r\n116:     prompt_parts.append(\"=\" * 100)\r\n117:     prompt_parts.append(\"🔒 PERSISTENT CANDIDATE CONTEXT (ALWAYS PRESENT - NEVER REMOVED):\")\r\n118:     prompt_parts.append(build_unlimited_candidate_profile(persistent_context, settings.PERSONALIZE_ANSWERS))\r\n119:     prompt_parts.append(\"=\" * 100)\r\n120:     \r\n121:     # Recent conversation history (limited to MAX_CONVERSATION_HISTORY exchanges)\r\n122:     if settings.INCLUDE_CONVERSATION_HISTORY and conversation_history:\r\n123:         prompt_parts.append(f\"📝 RECENT CONVERSATION HISTORY (LAST {settings.MAX_CONVERSATION_HISTORY} EXCHANGES FOR CONTEXT):\")\r\n124:         for i, exchange in enumerate(conversation_history, 1):\r\n125:             if exchange.get('interviewer_question'):\r\n126:                 prompt_parts.append(f\"Exchange {i} - INTERVIEWER: {exchange['interviewer_question']}\")\r\n127:             if exchange.get('candidate_response'):\r\n128:                 prompt_parts.append(f\"           ↳ CANDIDATE: {exchange['candidate_response']}\")\r\n129:             if exchange.get('ai_response'):\r\n130:                 # Include full AI response for complete context\r\n131:                 ai_response = exchange['ai_response']\r\n132:                 prompt_parts.append(f\"           ↳ AI ASSISTANT: {ai_response}\")\r\n133:             prompt_parts.append(\"\")\r\n134:         prompt_parts.append(\"=\" * 100)\r\n135:     \r\n136:     # Current question to answer\r\n137:     prompt_parts.append(\"🎯 CURRENT QUESTION TO ANSWER:\")\r\n138:     prompt_parts.append(f'\"{question}\"')\r\n139:     \r\n140:     # Enhanced Instructions with comprehensive markdown formatting\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":2118,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T04:54:30Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// Prompt builder matching Spectra interview intelligence\nfunction buildCandidateProfile(profile = {}) {\n    const parts = [];\n    if (profile.candidate_name) parts.push(`Candidate Name: ${profile.candidate_name}`);\n    if (profile.target_company) parts.push(`Target Company: ${profile.target_company}`);\n    if (profile.target_role) parts.push(`Target Role: ${profile.target_role}`);\n    if (profile.focus_areas && profile.focus_areas.length) {\n        parts.push(`Interview Focus Areas: ${profile.focus_areas.join(', ')}`);\n    }\n    if (profile.complete_resume) {\n        parts.push(`COMPLETE RESUME/BACKGROUND:\\n${profile.complete_resume}`);\n    }\n    if (profile.complete_job_description) {\n        parts.push(`COMPLETE JOB DESCRIPTION/REQUIREMENTS:\\n${profile.complete_job_description}`);\n    }\n    return parts.length ? parts.join('\\n') + '\\n' : '';\n}\n\nfunction getInterviewAnswerPrompt(question, persistentContext = {}, conversationHistory = []) {\n    const parts = [];\n\n    parts.push(`You are an expert interview coach providing real-time assistance during a live job interview.\nYour goal is to help the candidate give the best possible answer to the interviewer's question.\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n- Give a direct, high-impact answer. No fluff, no introductory chit-chat.\n- If technical/coding: provide clear algorithm steps, complexity (Time & Space), and clean code.\n- If behavioral: use the STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result) concisely.\n- If system design: cover requirements, high-level architecture, key trade-offs, and scaling.\n- Keep formatting clean using markdown bullet points and bold headers.`);\n\n    const profileText = buildCandidateProfile(persistentContext);\n    if (profileText) {\n        parts.push(\"=================================================================================\");\n        parts.push(\"PERSISTENT CANDIDATE CONTEXT:\");\n        parts.push(profileText);\n        parts.push(\"=================================================================================\");\n    }\n\n    if (conversationHistory && conversationHistory.length > 0) {\n        parts.push(\"RECENT CONVERSATION HISTORY:\");\n        const recent = conversationHistory.slice(-5);\n        recent.forEach((item, idx) => {\n            if (item.interviewer_question) parts.push(`Q${idx + 1}: ${item.interviewer_question}`);\n            if (item.ai_response) parts.push(`A${idx + 1}: ${item.ai_response.slice(0, 300)}...`);\n        });\n        parts.push(\"=================================================================================\");\n    }\n\n    parts.push(`CURRENT INTERVIEWER QUESTION:\n\"${question}\"\n\nProvide the answer for the candidate to speak right now:`);\n\n    return parts.join('\\n\\n');\n}\n\nfunction getVisionPrompt(userPrompt, persistentContext = {}) {\n    return `You are an expert technical interview assistant analyzing a screen capture from a live interview or coding test.\nThe candidate needs quick, accurate, actionable help.\n\n${userPrompt ? `USER REQUEST: \"${userPrompt}\"` : 'Analyze the code or problem shown on the screen, identify any bugs, provide the optimal solution, and explain clearly.'}\n\nFormat your answer with clean markdown, code snippets, and complexity analysis.`;\n}\n\nmodule.exports = {\n    buildCandidateProfile,\n    getInterviewAnswerPrompt,\n    getVisionPrompt\n};\n","Description":"Create prompt generation engine for interview and vision analysis","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\electron\\server\\prompts.js","toolAction":"Writing prompts.js","toolSummary":"Create prompts.js"}}]}
